WEBVTT

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:11.380
I'll hang onto this, too.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:15.260
Happy birthday!

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:19.140
She can have my wallet,
but not that bookmark!

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.520
Smells like... a woman...

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:39.580
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:49.060
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:54.030
"Episode 6"
"The Bad Girl"

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:01.660
There she is.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:07.080
Ah, Ryo, you're back!

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.710
Welcome home, sis!

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:14.550
Well? I toldja the Shima place'd
be lousy with cash!

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:15.760
What'd you get?

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:19.380
Don't do this in front of my brothers!

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:23.140
Besides, this is for us to <i>live </i>on!

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:25.100
Aw, c'mon!

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:29.140
--You oughta do as your father says.
--Some father <i>you </i>are!

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:31.440
Making your daughter do this stuff

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:33.940
while <i>you </i>just drink all day long!

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:39.740
Watch how you talk to your father!

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:43.990
Sis!

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:45.330
--Sis!
--Sis!

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:48.710
Tch! Is that all?

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:51.210
Why didn't you filch real <i>stacks </i>o' cash?

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:55.300
Give that back! The boys need that to eat!

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.670
Shaddap!

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:59.300
Daddy! Stop that!

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:05.560
Silence! I don't have time
to deal with you.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:08.890
It's you brats' fault for bein'
so damn useless!

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:10.270
--Don't hit our sister!

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:10.770
--I'm ashamed of myself...
--Don't hit our sister!

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:13.520
--I'm ashamed of myself...
--Shaddap!

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:21.320
You're back!

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:24.870
Yuzu...

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:27.410
You were late--I was worried.

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:31.540
Here: I put the caramels in a new jar.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:33.960
I cleaned up the old shattered one, too.

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:39.710
I'm going to bed.

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:40.720
Huh?

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:56.360
Today was my birthday and
Yuzu tried to celebrate, but...

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:59.360
I guess my birthday

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:01.150
never means anything good.

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:15.210
If you're up for it, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>,

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:18.290
shall we visit the Inari shrine
up the mountain again today?

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:21.920
Sorry. I have something
to take care of today.

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:25.220
Oh... oh, I see.

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:27.470
Thanks for breakfast.

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:28.930
Seconds?

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:29.930
I'm good.

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:42.320
I'll get that bookmark back today,
come hell or high water.

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:46.910
Though I <i>do </i>hope
her father's not around...

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:51.790
Begging your pardon!

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:00.420
I-Is no one home?

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:04.300
Sis, Sis! Look!

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:07.970
Hey! I told you to behave!

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:10.350
Look: a water pistol!

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:13.060
--Hah! See?
--Ah!

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:14.640
--Hah! See?
--<i>They're </i>in good spirits.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.100
Take that!

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:18.400
You hurry up and play, too, Sis!

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:28.570
Wha--what are <i>you </i>staring at, you jerk?!

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:33.200
I... I'm sorry.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:37.420
I didn't mean to see anything.

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:40.670
A-And I'm nearsighted--
I didn't see much anyway!

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:42.840
One hundred yen.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:44.010
Eh?

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:48.430
You beheld a fair maiden
of 18 years, bathing.

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:51.550
A hundred yen is a bargain.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:52.760
Pay up!

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:57.440
What do you mean?!
You <i>do </i>realize <i>you </i>have my wallet!

00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:58.520
Tch!

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:02.110
Aw, I really messed up.

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:05.110
Rumor has it you're a
gloomy rich-boy shut-in,

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:08.610
so I figured you'd just
cry yourself to sleep.

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:10.200
She's scary!

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:13.910
The way she talks and
acts--and picks a fight...

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:17.120
She's a bad girl--a real delinquent!

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:21.380
So? What is it?
Did you come for your wallet?

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:22.750
No, I didn't!

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:23.750
Huh?

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:26.920
The bookmark! The one you stole?

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:28.720
I want it back.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:30.010
Bookmark?

00:06:30.010 --> 00:06:32.760
It has pressed bellflowers on it!

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:35.180
It's very important to me.

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:36.890
--So--
--Sis!

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:40.400
Hey...

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:44.570
I don't understand this. Can you show me?

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.360
"Primary School" "Arithmetic Textbook"
Let's see here...

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:52.280
Sorry, Ryotaro--I'm no good at arithmetic.

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:53.410
What?!

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:59.580
But Richboy here said
he'll show you instead.

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:00.580
Huh?

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:06.300
He reads all kinds of books
and knows just about everything.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:08.880
"Primary School" "Arithmetic Textbook"
Really?! Wow, Richboy!

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:12.390
You <i>will </i>help him out, won't you?

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:15.010
Aha! So you <i>do </i>have it!

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:19.270
And who knows what'll happen
to it if you drop the ball?

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:22.980
Show me.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:24.650
Hooray!

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:26.860
There's a good boy.

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:29.440
So you have to carry this here.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:32.360
Oh, I get it! In other words, um...

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:37.370
I got roped into
teaching the lot of them.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:41.160
But it's all for the bookmark.
What choice do I have?

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:45.290
Why are you so obsessed
with this bookmark, anyway?

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:48.300
The girl who's going to
be my wife one day...

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:53.180
She made that--said the
flower reminded her of me.

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:57.510
It's valuable to me--irreplaceable.

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:06.650
Huh...

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:11.820
"A+"

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:11.820
Look, Richboy! Look at my paper!

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:14.410
"Taisho"

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:14.410
A-And my calligraphy!

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:17.330
He's looking at <i>my </i>work right now!

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:19.540
Yamato and Keita, you wait!

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:20.660
Aw!

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:23.420
No fair! It can't be just you!

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:27.380
An A-plus? That's fantastic!

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:29.250
It's written well, all right.

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:30.380
Really?!

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:33.130
"Taisho"

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:33.130
Such beautiful characters.

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:34.800
"Taisho"

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:34.800
Nice brushwork, too.

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:38.640
"Big Sis"

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:38.640
And look at my drawing, too!

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:40.140
Mine, too!

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:43.100
All done, Richboy! Did I get 'em right?

00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:46.310
Whoa, one at a time! Take turns!

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:50.190
Isn't it nice having Richboy
look at your work?

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:51.190
Yeah!

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:56.320
I <i>do </i>have a name: Tamahiko Shima.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:58.280
Please, stop with the "Richboy."

00:08:58.280 --> 00:08:59.910
"Tapioca shamer"?

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:03.750
"Tapioca"!

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:05.670
Mmm, yummy!

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:10.050
No! Ta-ma-hi-ko Shi-ma!

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:14.420
All right, let's call it a day.

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:19.260
Thank you very much, sensei!

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:21.600
"Sensei"...

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:24.560
You're pretty good, Tamahiko!

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:26.060
Just give me that bookmark!

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:28.730
Hey! I'm home!

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:31.520
Rats--it's Dad.

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:34.400
Go out the back. If he finds you,
you'll get a beating.

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:35.900
G-Got it.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:42.410
Hey! The bookmark?

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:43.830
I'll give it back later!

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:49.750
Hmm? Did we have us a guest?

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:51.630
N-No, not really...

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:57.970
I never got it back after all.

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:02.560
I don't know how I'll
be able to face Yuzu...

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:16.780
Welcome home!

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:18.570
The bath is ready for you.

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:20.700
Oh--did you want to eat first?

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:23.540
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>?

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:25.660
"sting sting"

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:25.660
Yuzu's kindness actually pains me now...

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:29.830
Sorry--I'm utterly exhausted.

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:34.210
It's straight to bed again for me tonight.

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:53.360
Couldn't sleep a wink.

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:57.900
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>, it's morning!

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:03.160
Do I go back to the way I used to be?

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:04.160
No--

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:07.200
I'll come clean to Yuzu.

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:10.460
Good morning, Tamahiko! You up?

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:12.830
One moment!

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:14.460
That voice...

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:19.800
Hey, Tamahiko!

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:21.930
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>...

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:26.510
Say, is this the girl who
was bought with money?

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:30.390
Come to think of it,
I've seen her in the village.

00:11:30.390 --> 00:11:33.060
So you like them little, huh?

00:11:34.810 --> 00:11:37.230
Watch how you talk about her!

00:11:37.230 --> 00:11:38.530
Yuzu is...

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:41.950
She's a good girl--far too good
for the likes of me!

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:50.370
I can see that.

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:54.790
She may be perfect--but <i>only</i>
for looking after you at home.

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:00.880
That scent...

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:05.010
Out <i>there</i>, you ought to be having
fun with <i>me</i>--your mistress.

00:12:05.010 --> 00:12:06.550
--Huh?!
--C'mon!

00:12:06.550 --> 00:12:08.680
Why try to hide it?

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:11.390
We were together all day
yesterday, after all.

00:12:11.390 --> 00:12:12.850
That's because you--

00:12:12.850 --> 00:12:15.980
Why, you were <i>thrilled</i>
to see my naked body!

00:12:15.980 --> 00:12:17.520
I was not, either!

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:20.690
And what's more...

00:12:20.690 --> 00:12:23.280
You gave me this bookmark, remember?

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:25.660
Said I was just like these flowers.

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:30.040
That is enough!

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:31.830
No more of your lies!

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:33.620
Give me back that bookmark!

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:38.550
What? Sure, if you make me your
mistress and let me live the high life!

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:39.670
Give it back!

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:43.800
Tch!

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:51.220
Yuzu!

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:54.600
Everything this delinquent says is a lie!

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:56.400
You mustn't believe her!

00:12:56.400 --> 00:13:00.280
She's the one who stole this
bookmark--along with my wallet!

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:10.540
Surely there were unavoidable
circumstances, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>.

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:16.580
I believe you.

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:26.680
Oh, dear me...

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:30.430
So we'll let this be the end of it.

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:33.730
Yuzu!

00:13:42.570 --> 00:13:43.570
Yuzu...

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:50.080
Aw, your precious bookmark
got all torn up.

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:54.660
<i>That </i>certainly didn't need to happen.

00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:56.120
Leave.

00:13:56.120 --> 00:13:57.040
Hmm?

00:13:57.040 --> 00:13:58.290
Leave.

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:02.090
Just... please. Leave.

00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:07.300
All right. See you later, Tamahiko.

00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:14.350
Now <i>that </i>was amusing!

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:21.060
She sure does act happy for
someone who was bought.

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:26.490
Well, guess I'd better get
home and feed those kids!

00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:46.210
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>? I'm coming in!

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:50.260
Breakfast is ready.

00:14:52.510 --> 00:14:53.430
What's this?

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:57.560
Whoops! You'll want to
change first, of course.

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:18.960
It's not bothering her?

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:23.130
Was that all it took to settle the matter?

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:30.380
Th-That's the telephone, right?

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:32.470
It's in the storeroom!

00:15:32.470 --> 00:15:34.050
I'll go answer it!

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:35.220
Who could it be?

00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:39.060
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>, it's Tamako-<i>san</i>!

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:41.350
Tamako?

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:46.570
H-Hello?

00:15:46.570 --> 00:15:50.150
What took you so long, brother?!
Pick up faster!

00:15:51.030 --> 00:15:52.280
Yikes!

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:54.280
S-Sorry...

00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:56.160
How are things going?

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:58.790
Kobe is really a lovely place.

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:03.420
I've transferred to a girls' school
here--and I've made lots of friends.

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:05.920
I even hosted a tea party the other day!

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:09.590
Really! Good for you, Tamako.

00:16:09.590 --> 00:16:10.670
I know!

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:13.550
And we all baked cookies together!

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:18.010
You know Yuzu's caramels
and almond macarons?

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:21.270
I'll be teaching them how
to make <i>those</i>, too!

00:16:22.980 --> 00:16:27.440
Wait--I didn't call to tell you all <i>that</i>!

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:32.070
What? But she <i>did </i>just bust out talking...

00:16:32.070 --> 00:16:36.070
Sorry. What did you have to tell me, then?

00:16:36.070 --> 00:16:37.330
Hap...

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:41.160
Happy birthday, Tamahiko.

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:48.880
I-I fully intended to call
you on the first,

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:53.680
but I was too embarr--<i>busy</i>, so I'm late!

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:55.010
Thanks.

00:16:55.010 --> 00:16:59.100
Yuzu must have had a little
celebration for you, right?

00:16:59.100 --> 00:17:01.180
Yeah, well...

00:17:01.180 --> 00:17:02.640
Did something happen?

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:03.520
Huh?!

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:05.270
Don't bother hiding anything.

00:17:05.270 --> 00:17:08.770
I could hear the discouraged
note in Yuzu's voice,

00:17:08.770 --> 00:17:13.860
and you sure don't seem happy for someone
who had a party thrown for him.

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:14.860
Well...

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:19.030
So there you go.

00:17:19.030 --> 00:17:22.080
It doesn't seem to be
bothering Yuzu, but...

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:23.080
I see.

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:27.500
Did you ever think why,
of all the flowers,

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:31.090
she gave you bellflowers?

00:17:31.090 --> 00:17:32.090
Eh?

00:17:33.210 --> 00:17:35.130
They remind her of me.

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:43.020
The girls at school sometimes use flower
language to express their feelings.

00:17:43.020 --> 00:17:44.480
Flower language?

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:47.190
It's more emotional than
just saying things out loud.

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:52.150
Bellflower means "unchanging love."

00:17:54.070 --> 00:17:57.740
It's a flower I'd give my
own special someone.

00:17:57.740 --> 00:18:01.120
Yuzu must have given you
that with the sentiment

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:04.660
that she'd pledge her love to you forever.

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:07.370
Then for it not only to be stolen,

00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:10.040
but to wind up in another woman's hands...

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:14.920
Just thinking about it, the sheer
sadness--it's heartbreaking.

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:22.720
Brother? Are you listening?

00:18:27.270 --> 00:18:30.860
The bellflower means "unchanging love"?

00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:32.900
Expressing feelings with flower language?

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:38.150
Pledging her love... forever?

00:18:40.950 --> 00:18:45.370
Well, heck... that's <i>absolutely</i>
something Yuzu would do.

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:49.920
This bookmark, torn into shreds...

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:53.460
Happy birthday!

00:18:53.460 --> 00:18:57.840
Right now, it's nothing less
than Yuzu's own heart.

00:19:18.490 --> 00:19:22.200
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>? Dinner's ready.

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:25.870
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>?

00:19:25.870 --> 00:19:28.540
Oh, dear. You've nodded off.

00:19:28.540 --> 00:19:30.330
You'll catch a cold.

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:41.510
I fell asleep...

00:19:44.100 --> 00:19:47.810
You still have that, I see.

00:19:47.810 --> 00:19:52.190
You needn't hold onto it--
not in <i>that </i>state.

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:57.780
The bellflower means
"unchanging love," doesn't it?

00:19:57.780 --> 00:20:01.030
Then no matter what this looks like,

00:20:01.030 --> 00:20:03.740
the sentiment remains the same!

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:08.240
That's... what I think.

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:12.210
Let's see...

00:20:16.420 --> 00:20:18.840
I'm sorry!

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:23.010
Oh, what have I done? I'm sorry!

00:20:23.010 --> 00:20:27.390
Why are you apologizing?
You haven't done anything wrong!

00:20:27.390 --> 00:20:29.220
It's just...

00:20:29.220 --> 00:20:33.730
I wish you'd told me
right away that you'd lost it.

00:20:33.730 --> 00:20:37.520
You probably had my feelings at heart...

00:20:37.520 --> 00:20:41.570
You stopped eating your meals with me--

00:20:41.570 --> 00:20:44.820
I thought you were avoiding me,

00:20:44.820 --> 00:20:48.120
or that I'd cooked a dish you hated.

00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:52.710
I was so worried... and terribly lonely.

00:20:52.710 --> 00:20:56.130
Oh... what a fool I am.

00:20:57.340 --> 00:21:00.710
I apologize. I really am sorry.

00:21:00.710 --> 00:21:02.470
That's right!

00:21:02.470 --> 00:21:05.840
No more taking on everything yourself.

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:08.600
But what I find most unforgiveable

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:12.140
is getting friendly with such
a beautiful woman.

00:21:12.140 --> 00:21:15.230
I mean... you have me.

00:21:15.230 --> 00:21:16.860
You stinker.

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:22.820
"punch punch"

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:22.820
You're just awful--awful!

00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:25.570
I'm sorry--I'm really sorry.

00:21:25.570 --> 00:21:28.530
--And after I cooked up such a feast, too!
--I sat there and let Yuzu pummel me
until she was satisfied.

00:21:28.530 --> 00:21:32.200
--Grrr!
--I sat there and let Yuzu pummel me
until she was satisfied.

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:35.920
And then...

00:21:37.250 --> 00:21:38.250
It's finished!

00:21:39.380 --> 00:21:42.550
What... what do you think?

00:21:42.550 --> 00:21:45.260
Oh, my! It came out wonderfully!

00:21:48.010 --> 00:21:50.970
It smells like glue... and you.

00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:55.810
Did you know, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>?

00:21:55.810 --> 00:21:59.860
Bellflowers have another
meaning, too: "integrity."

00:22:00.860 --> 00:22:05.110
Isn't that your character to a T?

00:23:38.870 --> 00:23:43.340
Tamahiko-<i>sama </i>has begun helping
the village children with their lessons.

00:23:43.340 --> 00:23:46.420
Our home is suddenly so lively now!

00:23:46.420 --> 00:23:49.670
Do your very best, Tamahiko-<i>sensei</i>!
